---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="High-Velocity AI Screen Triage Testing" description="Project detail">
  <main class="page-shell project-detail-shell">
    <article class="project-detail">
      <div class="project-header">
        <a href="/projects" class="back-link"><span aria-hidden="true">←</span> All case studies</a>
        <h1>High-Velocity AI Screen Triage Testing</h1>
        <p class="project-intro">Evaluated how AI-supported triage workflows performed under high-volume, time-constrained conditions to inform product readiness and confidence.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="project-meta-grid">
        <div class="meta-item">
          <span class="meta-label">Client:</span>
          <span class="meta-value">AI product team</span>
        </div>
        <div class="meta-item">
          <span class="meta-label">Role:</span>
          <span class="meta-value">Experimental researcher</span>
        </div>
        <div class="meta-item">
          <span class="meta-label">Focus:</span>
          <span class="meta-value">Rapid testing, triage validation, risk analysis</span>
        </div>
        <div class="meta-item">
          <span class="meta-label">Preview:</span>
          <a href="#" class="meta-link">View project →</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="project-content">
        <section class="content-section">
          <h2>Testing AI-augmented decision-making under realistic operational conditions</h2>
          <p>Before releasing an AI-augmented triage workflow to production, the team needed evidence that it would perform reliably under real operational stress. We designed rapid experiments that simulated high-volume, time-constrained conditions and measured both accuracy and user confidence.</p>
          <p>The testing revealed areas where the AI could confidently augment human decision-making and areas where human oversight remained essential. This evidence-backed approach reduced risk and helped the team launch with confidence.</p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </article>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
